            <ArticleTitle>A painful trp can be a bonding experience.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>635-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The receptive field of the TRPA1 nociceptor is remarkably expansive when compared to other chemodetectors such as odorant receptors. The identification of a unique mechanism utilized by TRPA1 helps clarify how this protein can efficiently alert the cell to an array of reactive chemical agents, regardless of their structure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
